.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-graph 1  "graph " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-graph \- Print the import graph — as text, Graphviz, Mermaid or data
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx graph\fR [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-cycles\fR] [\fB\-\-focus\fR] [\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the import graph — as text, Graphviz, Mermaid or data
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
relaxed, standard, strict or pristine
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: One line per edge, grouped by importer
.IP \(bu 2
dot: Graphviz, for `dot \-Tsvg`
.IP \(bu 2
mermaid: A fenced block GitHub and most wikis render on the spot
.IP \(bu 2
json: Nodes and edges as data
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-cycles\fR
Only the edges that close a cycle
.TP
\fB\-\-focus\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Only what this file reaches, and what reaches it
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR [default: 2]
How far from `\-\-focus` to follow
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads. Defaults to the machine\*(Aqs parallelism
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `RQX.toml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Leave the mouse to the terminal. Capture takes drag\-select away from it, and not every emulator passes shift+drag through
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx graph \-\-cycles                  only the rings
  rqx graph \-\-format mermaid          paste it into a design doc
  rqx graph \-\-focus src/api.ts        what it reaches, and what reaches it
